# Docker sends the whole context to the daemon before the build starts, and
# walks every file to do it. target/ is two gigabytes of build output that the
# image rebuilds from source anyway, so sending it buys nothing and costs the
# entire transfer.
#
# This matters for the named build contexts the miner and pool images use
# (--build-context avian-sv2=../avian-sv2). Building through
# scripts/stage-sources.sh in avian-sv2-deploy sidesteps it by exporting
# tracked files only, but building straight from a checkout does not.
target/

# Not read by any build here: nothing uses git describe or a vergen-style
# build script.
.git/
.gitignore

*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
